1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,897
This tutorial reads a renter's account the
way an accountant does.

2
00:00:04,897 --> 00:00:09,795
Open Finance and choose Tenant Ledger,
then select the prepared renter.

3
00:00:09,795 --> 00:00:14,247
RentAxis shows one block per ledger
account the renter has

4
00:00:14,247 --> 00:00:18,254
touched, and inside each block one row per
entry.

5
00:00:18,254 --> 00:00:23,152
Every row carries the document date, the
document number, the account

6
00:00:23,152 --> 00:00:27,604
on the other side of the entry, the
narration, the

7
00:00:27,604 --> 00:00:32,056
debit or the credit, and the running
balance after it.

8
00:00:32,056 --> 00:00:33,837
Start with rent receivable.

9
00:00:33,837 --> 00:00:38,289
The tenancy contract debited it with the
whole contract value,

10
00:00:38,289 --> 00:00:42,296
then one post-dated cheque entry per
cheque credited it

11
00:00:42,296 --> 00:00:46,303
back, so immediately after posting the
balance is zero.

12
00:00:46,303 --> 00:00:51,201
That is correct and it is the point: what
the renter

13
00:00:51,201 --> 00:00:55,653
owes lives in the cheque register, not in
this account.

14
00:00:55,653 --> 00:00:59,660
A balance appears here only when something
goes wrong,

15
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:03,667
such as a returned cheque, which debits it
again.

16
00:01:03,667 --> 00:01:06,338
Read the post-dated cheques receivable
block.

17
00:01:06,338 --> 00:01:11,236
It rises with every cheque registered and
falls with every cheque

18
00:01:11,236 --> 00:01:16,133
cleared, so its balance is the paper you
are still holding.

19
00:01:16,133 --> 00:01:17,469
Read advance rent.

20
00:01:17,469 --> 00:01:22,811
The contract credited the whole year, and
each month-end recognition debits back

21
00:01:22,811 --> 00:01:28,154
the portion earned, so it winds down to
zero across the term.

22
00:01:28,154 --> 00:01:32,606
Select any document number to open the
journal behind it.

23
00:01:32,606 --> 00:01:36,613
A journal shows every line, always
balancing, and it

24
00:01:36,613 --> 00:01:40,175
cannot be edited or deleted, only
reversed, which

25
00:01:40,175 --> 00:01:43,737
writes a mirror entry and links the two.

26
00:01:43,737 --> 00:01:45,518
Finally open Trial Balance.

27
00:01:45,518 --> 00:01:50,415
Choose a date and confirm that total
debits equal total credits.

28
00:01:50,415 --> 00:01:54,422
That single check is what tells you the
ledger

29
00:01:54,422 --> 00:01:57,984
behind every screen in this tutorial is
sound.
